# Frontend Integration Skills (2025–2026)

## How to Use This File

This file catalogs 20 foundational-to-advanced skills specific to frontend integration within Laravel. Each skill includes a concise definition, a real-world usage trigger, and a source reference.

When assisting users, match their request to the most relevant skill name and cite it when explaining recommendations. Always prefer Laravel 11 idioms for new code. Skills referencing Laravel 12/13 features are forward-awareness only -- do not use them unless the project has been upgraded.

Source URLs default to Laravel 11.x docs (the current project version). Where a feature is only documented in 13.x, the 13.x URL is noted as a forward reference.

## Skill Catalog

- **Blade Components (Anonymous & Class-Based)** — creates reusable UI fragments with slots, attributes, and scoped logic. *Use when:* extracting repeated markup, implementing design system tokens, or enabling theme customization. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/11.x/blade#components
- **Component Slots & Attribute Passthrough** — defines content injection points and forwards HTML attributes to child elements. *Use when:* building flexible layouts, supporting wrapper components, or enabling compositional UI patterns. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/11.x/blade#slots
- **Livewire 3 Lifecycle Hooks** — responds to component mount, update, and render events for reactive server-side logic. *Use when:* implementing real-time forms, dynamic filters, or progressive enhancement without SPA complexity. *Source:* https://livewire.laravel.com/docs/3.x/lifecycle
- **wire:model.live & Deferred Binding (Livewire 3+)** — controls when input changes sync to server via live, blur, or deferred modes. *Use when:* optimizing network usage, implementing instant search, or reducing server load for frequent updates. *Source:* https://livewire.laravel.com/docs/3.x/properties
- **Computed Properties & wire:loading (Livewire 3)** — derives reactive values and shows loading states during async operations. *Use when:* formatting display values, calculating aggregates, or providing UX feedback during requests. *Source:* https://livewire.laravel.com/docs/3.x/properties
- **Full-Page Components & wire:navigate (Livewire 3)** — enables SPA-like navigation with server-rendered pages and prefetching. *Use when:* building admin panels, dashboards, or content sites requiring fast client-side transitions. *Source:* https://livewire.laravel.com/docs/3.x/navigation
- **Inertia.js v2 Foundation (SPA + Laravel Routing)** — bridges Vue or React SPAs to Laravel controllers and routes without a separate API layer. *Use when:* building modern SPAs that reuse Laravel's auth, validation, and routing, or migrating Blade apps to a JS-first frontend incrementally. *Source:* https://inertiajs.com
- **Inertia.js v2 Async Requests & Polling** — enables non-blocking page loads, background data refresh, and deferred prop loading. *Use when:* building interactive SPAs with Laravel controllers, implementing infinite scroll, or reducing payload size. *Source:* training
- **Deferred Props & Prefetching (Inertia 2+)** — loads expensive data after initial render or pre-fetches likely next pages. *Use when:* optimizing perceived performance, reducing server load for optional data, or enabling seamless navigation. *Source:* training
- **Vue 3 Composition API & Reactivity** — uses ref, computed, and watch for fine-grained reactive state management. *Use when:* building complex client-side interactions, sharing logic via composables, or integrating with Inertia. *Source:* training
- **React 18 Hooks & Concurrent Features** — leverages useState, useEffect, and transitions for responsive UIs. *Use when:* implementing dynamic forms, real-time updates, or integrating with Laravel APIs via Inertia. *Source:* training
- **Vite Configuration & HMR** — bundles assets with hot module replacement for rapid frontend development. *Use when:* developing with Vue/React, optimizing production builds, or managing CSS/JS dependencies. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/11.x/vite
- **Frontend Asset Optimization (Lazy Loading, WebP, CDN)** — improves Core Web Vitals via deferred image loading, modern image formats, and edge delivery. *Use when:* tuning LCP/CLS, reducing bandwidth on image-heavy pages, or preparing apps for production traffic. *Source:* training
- **Tailwind CSS Utility-First Styling** — applies responsive, theme-aware classes directly in markup for rapid UI development. *Use when:* prototyping interfaces, maintaining design consistency, or enabling JIT compilation. *Source:* https://tailwindcss.com
- **Vanilla ES6+ Modules & Async Patterns** — uses native imports, async/await, and fetch for lightweight client logic. *Use when:* avoiding framework overhead, enhancing Blade pages progressively, or integrating with Livewire. *Source:* training
- **AJAX Patterns with CSRF Handling** — sends asynchronous requests with proper token inclusion and error handling. *Use when:* building dynamic forms, implementing live search, or updating UI without full page reloads. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/11.x/csrf
- **JSON Contracts & Type Safety** — defines shared interfaces for API request/response shapes between frontend and backend. *Use when:* enabling TypeScript integration, preventing runtime errors, or documenting client expectations. *Source:* training
- **SPA Authentication Flows** — manages session cookies vs. token storage, refresh logic, and protected route handling. *Use when:* building Inertia/Vue/React apps with Laravel Sanctum or Passport. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/11.x/sanctum
- **Client-Side Validation & Error Display** — mirrors server validation rules in frontend for immediate user feedback. *Use when:* improving UX, reducing roundtrips, or ensuring form completeness before submission. *Source:* training
- **Form Handling with Livewire/Inertia** — binds form state, handles submission, and displays validation errors reactively. *Use when:* building complex multi-step forms, implementing real-time validation, or reducing boilerplate. *Source:* training

## Project-Specific Admin UI Design Tokens

### Color Palette
- **Primary** (blue): `btn-info`, `bg-primary` — View action, stat cards
- **Success** (green): `btn-success`, `bg-success` — Edit action, stat cards
- **Danger** (red): `btn-danger`, `bg-danger` — Delete action, stat cards
- **Warning** (yellow): `bg-warning` — Stat cards
- **Info** (teal): `btn-teal` — Restore action
- **Secondary** (gray): `btn-secondary` — Back/reset buttons

### Spacing
- Card body padding: `p-3`
- Row gap: `g-3` in Bootstrap grid
- Section spacing: `mb-4` between major sections

### Icon Set
- Use Tabler Icons (`ti ti-{name}`) for all admin UI icons
- Common icons: `eye`, `pencil`, `trash`, `refresh`, `arrow-left`, `user`, `mail`, `phone`, `settings`, `dashboard`, `list`, `plus`, `filter`, `search`, `download`

### Typography
- Card headers: `h5` with `mb-0`
- Stat values: `h3` with `mb-0`
- Labels: `fw-bold text-muted`
- Body: default Bootstrap size

### Admin View Paths
- Show views: `resources/views/admin/{section}/show.blade.php`
- Detail partials: `resources/views/admin/admins/parts/detail-row.blade.php`, `file-detail-row.blade.php`
- Form components: `resources/views/components/form/`
- CSS overrides: `public/style/admin/css/filter.css`

### Template Reference
- Show view template: `.cursor/templates/show-view-template.md`
- Table view template: `.cursor/templates/table-view-template.md`
- Full standards doc: `.cursor/styles/admin-ui-standards.md`